# Git: commit only, never push

- You may run **`git add`** and **`git commit`** when the user wants work saved to version control.
- **Do not run `git push`**, `git push origin`, or any command that updates the remote (including `gh pr create` if it implies push, unless the user explicitly asks to push in that message).
- The human reviews commits locally and pushes to GitHub when they choose.

If the user explicitly says to push in the same request, follow their explicit instruction for that turn only.
